WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.479
The page carries a receipt: a hash of the dossier behind the story.

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:16.031
A hash ties the story to the record. Same file, same value, checkable by someone else.

00:00:16.031 --> 00:00:24.024
The full value stays on the page. It is there to compare, not to memorise.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:32.195
The hash identifies the record. It does not prove that the record is complete.

00:00:32.195 --> 00:00:40.416
It does not prove correctness. A matching hash can still sit beside a weak claim.

00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:47.372
The locator still matters. Open the evidence and read the limit.

00:00:47.372 --> 00:00:52.146
Check the hash, then check the findings.

00:00:52.146 --> 00:00:58.196
A receipt is a start. It is not the whole argument.
